;; The library's own coordinates, and the only place they are written.
;;
;; com.kirahowe.secrets.release, the release guards under build/, reads this
;; file from the repository. com.kirahowe.secrets.init, which ships in the jar,
;; reads it as a classpath resource. So what a release checks and what the
;; initializer writes into a consumer's project cannot be edited apart.
;;
;; :version is the release being built. :git is the last *released* tag and the
;; commit it names, which is what the initializer scaffolds until a Maven
;; artifact exists to point at instead. It lags :version by construction: a
;; commit cannot contain its own hash, so the pin can only move after the
;; release it names has been tagged.
{:lib com.kirahowe/secrets
 :version "0.1.0"
 :git {:lib io.github.kirahowe/secrets
       :tag "v0.1.0"
       :sha "89ded34ce8bd146754cc3ec9971d1ea1fd25da28"}}
